// Home Lab tailnet policy — Phase 13 §6.7. Applied by hand in the admin console:
//   https://login.tailscale.com/admin/acls/file
// Configuration, not a secret (brief §9). Tailscale SSH stays declined (ADR-019):
// the default "ssh" block is removed on purpose — tailscaled runs without --ssh
// and nothing should suggest otherwise.
//
// What this does: any device logged in as a member of this (single-user) tailnet
// may reach the node on TCP 22, and nothing else may reach the node at all.
// Before Phase 13 the policy was the stock {"src":["*"],"dst":["*"],"ip":["*"]}.
//
// What it does NOT do: it is a device-level boundary in FRONT of sshd, not a
// replacement for it. Keys still authenticate (ADR-018). WireGuard/DERP transport
// on UDP 41641 is not subject to grants. A new listener that must be reachable
// from the MacBook (e.g. Phase 23.0's endpoint if it is not tunnelled) gets its
// port added to the "ip" list here in the same commit as its socket-table row.
//
// Recovery: a wrong policy locks the MacBook out of the node while leaving the
// node itself fine. Fix it from any browser at the URL above; the console
// (ADR-041) is the fallback if the MacBook cannot reach anything.
{
	"hosts": {
		"homelab": "100.71.62.71",
	},

	"grants": [
		{"src": ["autogroup:member"], "dst": ["homelab"], "ip": ["tcp:22"]},
	],

	// No "tests" block: the console rejects autogroup:member as a test source
	// ("unknown user or host", OBSERVED 2026-09-12) and the single-user tailnet
	// has no other principal to name without committing an e-mail address.
	// The proof is the runbook's nc: port 22 answers, port 2222 times out.
}
